  "description": "Unique vertex- and edge-minimal counterexample to Conjecture 5.2 across all finite simple graphs with Delta(G) <= 3: a 15-vertex, 14-edge subcubic tree F_3 formed by chaining three 5-vertex units V_i = {h_i, l1_i, l2_i, a_i, b_i} via edges (l2_0, l1_1) and (l2_1, l1_2) (shown here in canonical vertex numbering). Exhaustive enumeration of all 1,375,631 non-isomorphic connected graphs with Delta(G) <= 3 and n <= 15 proves zero counterexamples exist for n <= 14 (358,891 graphs) and exactly three exist at n = 15 (this unique tree CE#1 plus two 15-edge unicyclic graphs CE#2 and CE#3 on which the static model globally strictly dominates the sequential model).",
